{"type":"agent_end","messages":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Using this dataset's total farmers markets, and the census file: how many farmers markets does the U.S. have per 100,000 residents, to four decimal places? One confident sentence. Do not mention unverified facts and use tools to do any math necessary. Data sources: https://harvestlymarkets.com/data/us-farmers-markets-by-state-2026.csv and https://gist.githubusercontent.com/hussainsultan/369600f5179b22792a2b4c9ed37de056/raw/NST-EST2025-ALLDATA.csv"}],"timestamp":1786915205895},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user is asking me to:\n1. Get the total number of farmers markets from the first dataset\n2. Get the total U.S. population from the census file\n3. Calculate farmers markets per 100,000 residents to 4 decimal places\n4. Provide one confident sentence with this verified answer\n\nFollowing the xorq analyst protocol, I need to:\n1. First check `xorq_semantic_models` to see if there are any pre-computed models\n2. Then `xorq_catalog_list_aliases` to see what's available\n3. If not available, I need to ingest the two CSV sources into the catalog\n4. Then use `xorq_select` to get the numbers\n5. Finally use `xorq_verify` to verify the answer\n\nLet me start by checking what's in the catalog.","thinkingSignature":""},{"type":"text","text":"I'll help you calculate the farmers markets per 100,000 residents. Let me start by checking what's available in the catalog and then ingest these data sources if needed."},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_01BK9xoPXU2zJnL6b1D76oMp","name":"xorq_semantic_models","arguments":{"catalog_path":".xorq/catalog"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_015X4LkSwg4ZpApzQMTks2Jh","name":"xorq_catalog_list_aliases","arguments":{"catalog_path":".xorq/catalog"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"anthropic","model":"claude-haiku-4-5","usage":{"input":10,"output":346,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":8157,"totalTokens":8513,"cost":{"input":0.000009999999999999999,"output":0.0017300000000000002,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0.01019625,"total":0.01193625},"cacheWrite1h":0,"reasoning":192},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1786915205916,"responseId":"msg_011Ce78HjhTkyw3Sw8HFepfE","rawStopReason":"tool_use"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_01BK9xoPXU2zJnL6b1D76oMp","toolName":"xorq_semantic_models","content":[{"type":"text","text":"No semantic models in this catalog — fall back to the ordinary ingest/compose flow."}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1786915209800},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_015X4LkSwg4ZpApzQMTks2Jh","toolName":"xorq_catalog_list_aliases","content":[{"type":"text","text":"No aliases.\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1786915209800},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The catalog is empty, so I need to ingest both CSV sources. Let me create the build scripts to load both datasets into the catalog. Following the xorq-catalog skill instructions, I need to:\n\n1. Create `.xorq/scripts/farmers-markets.py` to load the first CSV\n2. Create `.xorq/scripts/census-population.py` to load the second CSV\n3. Build both\n4. Add them to the catalog\n5. Then compose a metric that calculates farmers markets per 100,000 residents\n6. Query and verify\n\nLet me start by creating the scripts directory and the build scripts.","thinkingSignature":""},{"type":"text","text":"The catalog is empty. I need to ingest both datasets. Let me create the build scripts for each data source."},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_01JfuwVoFYvS9C7FNiEdRhMn","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"mkdir -p .xorq/scripts"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_018ECUp1hvAvmuVEKMHAGEie","name":"write","arguments":{"path":".xorq/scripts/farmers-markets.py","content":"import xorq.operators as xo\nfrom frozendict import FrozenDict\n\nexpr = xo.deferred_read_csv(\n    \"https://harvestlymarkets.com/data/us-farmers-markets-by-state-2026.csv\",\n    con=None,\n    storage_options=FrozenDict({\"User-Agent\": \"xorq-analyst\"}),\n)\n"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_01BMrc9QoqxLANFnAwSNjqRv","name":"write","arguments":{"path":".xorq/scripts/census-population.py","content":"import xorq.operators as xo\nfrom frozendict import FrozenDict\n\nexpr = xo.deferred_read_csv(\n    \"https://gist.githubusercontent.com/hussainsultan/369600f5179b22792a2b4c9ed37de056/raw/NST-EST2025-ALLDATA.csv\",\n    con=None,\n    storage_options=FrozenDict({\"User-Agent\": \"xorq-analyst\"}),\n)\n"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"anthropic","model":"claude-haiku-4-5","usage":{"input":14,"output":566,"cacheRead":8157,"cacheWrite":443,"totalTokens":9180,"cost":{"input":0.000014,"output":0.00283,"cacheRead":0.0008157,"cacheWrite":0.00055375,"total":0.0042134500000000005},"cacheWrite1h":0,"reasoning":144},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1786915209801,"responseId":"msg_011Ce78J4Ai8Cq7kVbnJjwgC","rawStopReason":"tool_use"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_01JfuwVoFYvS9C7FNiEdRhMn","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"(no output)"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1786915214571},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_018ECUp1hvAvmuVEKMHAGEie","toolName":"write","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Successfully wrote 250 bytes to .xorq/scripts/farmers-markets.py"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1786915214571},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_01BMrc9QoqxLANFnAwSNjqRv","toolName":"write","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Successfully wrote 289 bytes to .xorq/scripts/census-population.py"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1786915214571},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I need to build both scripts using xorq build command.","thinkingSignature":""},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_01KPpJiCouJvwTgxGAHdZSC6","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"cd .xorq && xorq build scripts/farmers-markets.py --builds-dir builds --emit-build-path-to /tmp/fm_bp.txt && cat /tmp/fm_bp.txt"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_01RJbcCPiFb2hRfdXbpsMs2j","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"cd .xorq && xorq build scripts/census-population.py --builds-dir builds --emit-build-path-to /tmp/cp_bp.txt && cat /tmp/cp_bp.txt"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"anthropic","model":"claude-haiku-4-5","usage":{"input":14,"output":203,"cacheRead":8600,"cacheWrite":696,"totalTokens":9513,"cost":{"input":0.000014,"output":0.001015,"cacheRead":0.0008600000000000001,"cacheWrite":0.00087,"total":0.002759},"cacheWrite1h":0,"reasoning":19},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1786915214572,"responseId":"msg_011Ce78JNfCgirTGQyqc1aUC","rawStopReason":"tool_use"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_01KPpJiCouJvwTgxGAHdZSC6","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Building expr from scripts/farmers-markets.py\nTraceback (most recent call last):\n  File \"/nix/store/yvlv6n4rx6dnnvhi7sgc5lm0152pa8mx-pi-xorq-duel-dev-env/lib/python3.13/site-packages/xorq/cli.py\", line 797, in invoke\n    return super().invoke(ctx)\n           ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~^^^^^\n  File \"/nix/store/yvlv6n4rx6dnnvhi7sgc5lm0152pa8mx-pi-xorq-duel-dev-env/lib/python3.13/site-packages/click/core.py\", line 1873, in invoke\n    return _process_result(sub_ctx.command.invoke(sub_ctx))\n                           ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~^^^^^^^^^\n  File \"/nix/store/yvlv6n4rx6dnnvhi7sgc5lm0152pa8mx-pi-xorq-duel-dev-env/lib/python3.13/site-packages/click/core.py\", line 1269, in invoke\n    return ctx.invoke(self.callback, **ctx.params)\n           ~~~~~~~~~~^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\n  File \"/nix/store/yvlv6n4rx6dnnvhi7sgc5lm0152pa8mx-pi-xorq-duel-dev-env/lib/python3.13/site-packages/click/core.py\", line 824, in invoke\n    return callback(*args, **kwargs)\n  File \"/nix/store/yvlv6n4rx6dnnvhi7sgc5lm0152pa8mx-pi-xorq-duel-dev-env/lib/python3.13/site-packages/xorq/cli.py\", line 1149, in build\n    build_command(\n    ~~~~~~~~~~~~~^\n        script_path,\n        ^^^^^^^^^^^^\n    ...<5 lines>...\n        emit_build_path_to=emit_build_path_to,\n        ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^